What are Speed Stacks?
Speed Stacks are a line of plastic cup stacking kits that have evolved from a casual pastime into a competitive sport. Each stack consists of precisely engineered plastic cups that snap together in a defined sequence, allowing participants to record fast completion times. The methodology tests hand-eye coordination, reaction time, and overall dexterity, making them popular in schools, community centres, and competitive leagues.
The design focuses on lightweight yet durable construction, ensuring a consistent bounce and minimal breakage across repeated use. Manufacturers often embed subtle branding, colour coding, and aesthetic elements that align with educational curricula or athletically themed programmes. The products range from six cup starter sets for elementary schools up to twelve cup premium models for professional leagues and high school championships.
